\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab Thou God of truth and love,
\par \pard\li720 We seek Thy perfect way,
\par Ready Thy choice to approve,
\par Thy providence to obey :
\par Enter into Thy wise design,
\par And sweetly lose our will in Thine.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab Why hast Thou cast our lot
\par \pard\li720 In the same age and place,
\par And why together brought
\par To se each other's face ;
\par To join with loving sympathy,
\par And mix our friendly souls in Thee ?
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab Didst Thou not make us one,
\par \pard\li720 That we might one remain,
\par Together travel on,
\par And bear each other's pain ;
\par Till all Thy utmost goodness prove,
\par And rise renewed in perfect love ?
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4\tab Then let us ever bear
\par \pard\li720 The blessed end in view,
\par And join, with mutual care,
\par To fight our passage through ;
\par And kindly help each other on,
\par Till all receive  the starry crown.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab O may Thy Spirit seal
\par \pard\li720 Our souls unto that day,
\par With all Thy fullness fill,
\par And then transport away :
\par Away to our eternal rest,
\par Away to our Redeemer's breast.
\par Amen 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

